WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.489 --> 00:00:05.980
Speaker 1: Let's now go to someone very different
than Chris Christie, and I'm talking about

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.250
Ron DeSantis.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:11.840
Ron DeSantis put forth a plan yesterday on
Fox News.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:18.960
So insane, so ridiculous and so deranged that
even Fox News host Martha MACCALLUM is visibly

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:22.170
skeptical and obviously doesn't buy it.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:28.170
DeSantis was asked whether he wants to eliminate
any agencies, and he mentioned not only three

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:34.239
entire agencies, departments, commerce, energy
and Education, but he said he would eliminate

00:00:34.239 --> 00:00:36.270
the IRS, which is so ridiculous.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:39.820
But then the thing he says after that is almost
worse.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:40.820
Take a listen.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.129
Speaker 2: Are you in favor of eliminating
any agencies?

00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:47.100
I know conservatives in the past have talked
about closing the Department of Education.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.199
Would you do that?

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:55.239
Speaker 3: So we would do education, we would
do commerce, we do energy, and we would do

00:00:55.239 --> 00:00:56.239
IRS.

00:00:56.239 --> 00:01:00.430
And so if Congress will work with me on doing
that, we'll be able to eliminate the size

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.309
and scope of government, but also going to
do more things.

00:01:03.309 --> 00:01:06.619
Be prepared if Congress won't go that far.

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:12.020
I'm going to use those agencies to push back
against woke ideology and against the leftism

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:15.220
that we see creeping in to all institutions
of American life.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:20.660
So, for example, with Department of Education,
we reverse all the transgender sports stuff.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.450
Women's sports should be protected.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.800
We reverse policies trying to inject the curriculum
into our schools.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:27.800
That will all be gone.

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:31.720
We will make sure we have an accreditation
system for higher ed, which is not trying

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.710
to foment more things like DII and CRT.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.190
So we'll be prepared to do both.

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:39.140
Either way, it'll be a win for conservatives.

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:45.930
Speaker 1: Imagine for a second if a Democratic
presidential candidate said, I will be using

00:01:45.930 --> 00:01:52.460
the IRS, the Department of Commerce, the Department
of Education, and the Department of Energy

00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:54.650
to destroy conservatism.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:02:00.070
Imagine for a second if a Democratic president
ever said something like that, they would

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:01.289
be calling for their head.

00:02:01.289 --> 00:02:04.080
They would be saying lock him or her up.

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:11.430
Rick Wilson tweeted, I'll either eliminate
these agencies or use them to destroy my political

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:12.440
enemies.

00:02:12.440 --> 00:02:16.470
Set every authoritarian in the history of
ever.

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.650
This is outrageous.

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.430
This is a dangerous extremist.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:24.400
And by the way, give me a break, dude.

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.500
This is in the style of the Trump promises.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:30.989
Anyone with any common sense knows it will
never happen.

00:02:30.989 --> 00:02:34.340
He's not going to get rid certainly he's not
going to get rid of the IRS.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.280
And I don't think if he was president, he
would get rid of the Department of Education

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:42.010
or the Department of Commerce or the Department
of Energy, which was the other one.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:46.030
This is sort of like Mexico is going to build
pay to build our wall across the entire U.S.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.209
Mexico border.

00:02:47.209 --> 00:02:48.209
And I will solve the U.

00:02:48.209 --> 00:02:50.810
At the Israeli-Palestinian conflict in my
first term.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.430
We all know you're not doing any of that.

00:02:52.430 --> 00:02:55.230
And after the fact, some people defend it
by saying, well, it was aspirational.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:58.000
That's what he wanted to do.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:03.350
Don't we want to hold our presidential candidates
in terms of the promises they make, at least

00:03:03.350 --> 00:03:06.980
to some degree, to things that are remotely
possible?

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:13.849
So this reminds me of the classic moment where
Rick Perry, during his failed bid for the

00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:18.400
Republican presidential nomination, also wanted
to remove a bunch of departments but forgot

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:19.400
which ones.

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.990
This is a classic, and I will tell you.

00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:24.879
Speaker 3: It is three agencies of government
when I get there that are gone.

00:03:24.879 --> 00:03:27.611
Is it commerce, Education and the.

00:03:27.611 --> 00:03:30.310
What's the third one there?

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:31.560
Let's see.

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:32.799
Oh five.

00:03:32.799 --> 00:03:33.799
Okay.

00:03:33.799 --> 00:03:37.530
So Commerce, Education and the EPA.

00:03:37.530 --> 00:03:38.560
EPA.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:42.680
Unidentified: There you go.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:43.709
No.

00:03:43.709 --> 00:03:44.739
Seriously.

00:03:44.739 --> 00:03:49.341
Is EPA what you were talking about?

00:03:49.341 --> 00:03:50.341
No, sir.

00:03:50.341 --> 00:03:51.341
No, sir.

00:03:51.341 --> 00:03:52.341
We were talking about the.

00:03:52.341 --> 00:03:53.341
Speaker 3: Agencies of government.

00:03:53.341 --> 00:03:54.341
The EPA needs to be rebuilt.

00:03:54.341 --> 00:03:55.341
Speaker 1: I don't know.

00:03:55.341 --> 00:03:56.341
Remove them all.

00:03:56.341 --> 00:03:58.130
Speaker 3: But you can't name the third one.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.130
The third agency of government.

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:00.130
I would.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.709
I would do away with the education.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:03.350
Unidentified: The commerce.

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:04.350
Commerce.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:07.569
Speaker 3: And let's see.

00:04:07.569 --> 00:04:08.980
I can't.

00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:11.010
Speaker 1: The third.

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.010
Sorry.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:13.010
Yeah.

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.730
Listen, they're not getting rid of any of
these things, but they are extraordinarily

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.030
dangerous people.

00:04:17.030 --> 00:04:20.720
And the fact that DeSantis is willing to say,
I'll get rid of the IRS, what we, of course,

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:27.430
need to do, if you actually want to take seriously
the idea of people who are not paying their

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:33.010
fair share and you actually need to you need
to scale up the IRS, need to give the IRS

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:35.590
the resources to actually conduct audits.

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:44.200
And we know that the multiplier effect, the
return on IRS audit agents to target extraordinarily

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.290
high income individuals is an extremely profitable
thing.

00:04:48.290 --> 00:04:53.120
And as I've said before, if you hire an irate
IRS agent for 70 grand and they're mostly

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.880
auditing people making 30 grand, even if those
people underpaid their taxes by ten or 15%,

00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.440
you're not going to recover very much money.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:05.600
But we know that the very rich, underpaid,
I don't mean underpaid from a political or

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:06.600
moral standpoint.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:10.111
I just mean they're not paying what the law
currently says they should pay based on the

00:05:10.111 --> 00:05:11.111
tax code.

00:05:11.111 --> 00:05:12.460
It's not legal loopholes.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.710
They're just they're just putting in the wrong
information.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.280
They're not paying what they should pay.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:18.590
Under current law.

00:05:18.590 --> 00:05:24.371
It's extremely profitable from the standpoint
of what you pay the IRS agents versus what

00:05:24.371 --> 00:05:27.740
you end up recovering and people who didn't
pay what they're supposed to pay.

00:05:27.740 --> 00:05:29.259
That's the direction we should go.

00:05:29.259 --> 00:05:30.530
Not getting rid of the IRS.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:32.350
But again, it's another one of these virtue
signals.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.350
IRS is now bad.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:36.840
It's political, it's, you know, armed agents,
blah, blah, blah.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:41.600
Ron DeSantis, even if he becomes president,
is not getting rid of the IRS.

